# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's core.autocrlf (#37).
#
# Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on Windows as on
# Linux. Cloud Build clones on Linux, so LF is what the pipeline sees; making
# every checkout match means an LF file written by any editor or tool adds
# cleanly, with no "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning, and a diff never
# shows a whole file rewritten because two machines disagreed.
#
# Nothing tracked needs CRLF: there are no .cmd or .bat files, and Windows
# PowerShell runs LF .ps1 scripts. If one is ever added, give it
# `eol=crlf` below rather than changing the default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never converted. text=auto already detects these, but naming
# the binary types in the tree removes the guess. Add a line when a new one
# is committed.
*.png   binary
*.woff2 binary
